                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Let's preface by saying this game is pretty good. It's extremely worth the price and worth a good 10-20 hours of game. \n\nBut for the game itself: It's a bit buggy sometimes, the exploration can be dizzingly confusing, and going for any obscure achievement is hard beyond belief if you just try looking by yourself. Even the guide can be unclear. All in all it's a bit messy. And there are a number of potential softlocks.\n\nHowever, it's an extremely charming game with a pleasing environment that challenges a casual player just enough. However, the real star of the show is the abilities. In particular, the standout few. Some abilities are useless or honestly just another ability but slightly different. but OH. MY. GOD. The fairy (default, so even in the pacifist run, you have an OP and extremely fun ability) and stone abilities make this game worth replaying over and over again. \n\nThe fairy is especially a novel ability unlike any other I've seen in a game. You'd think literally dropping your weapon would make for a poor design choice but NO. It's so genius how it forces you to to think about your movement and combat in such a complicated way. It feels incredible to land the right angle and the movement of the fairy can be janky, but it actually adds to the tech of the ability. It's the most memorable part of this game and I wish I could see more abilities like this in other metroidvanias or similar games.\n\nThe stone ability is just as good. It's a complex balance between spamming horizontal movement that zooms you across the map, gaining minimal height, your vulnerability when coming out of it at Mach 20, and it's actual combat power. It's an incredibly fun ability that is useful almost anywhere at the cost of you needing to know exactly what you're about to run into in a fraction of a second. It's a joy to traverse the map with this ability and just like the fairy, I wish more games could implement strong abilities like this where the only drawback is your reaction time. \n\nOther abilities are fun and useful, but the fairy and stone make this whole game worth it's weight in gold. 1000% a must play if you love unique movement abilities.",
